/-!
# Actual bundle identifications for the effective elliptic divisor

The independently constructed effective Cartier line bundle is
holomorphically, fibrewise complex-linearly identified with the original
canonical bundle on the entire order-four elliptic patch.  The map
preserves the literal base point and carries its canonical divisor
section to the actual canonical section on that patch.

On the actual complement of the central surface, its original `none`
trivialization gives a holomorphic fibre-linear product identification,
taking the divisor section to one.  Both identifications and their
inverses use the original bundle total-space topologies and atlases.
No global identification with the canonical bundle is asserted.
-/
